	(text "LMR33630BDDAR? 24V solid, 3A, 1.2Mhz, cheap and well stocked...\nLMR41420Y - 24V, 2A, 1.1Mhz, cheap and well stocked.\nSY8303 - 24v solid, 3A, 500-2000k, cheap and well stocked.\nI still refuse to use non-synch buck in the year of our wonder, 2026\nUsing two of the same, would save me extended fees, ok for small orders?\nbut just an 1117 is better?\n\n2 of them means you can always have 3.3v regardless of bus voltage?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 294.894 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "22d8730e-853a-415e-9627-311b25ada8e6")
	)
	(text "5-24V in, with\n buck to 12\n buck to 5\n buck to 3.3 (lol, no, who needs that)\n passthrough\nas options for the led supply.\nseparate 3.3V ~ish supply for the esp32 itself.\njust an ams1117-3.3 for the esp32? could I live with myself?"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 187.452 153.162 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "24c97331-1af1-4531-9a97-e6fd93c398e8")
	)
	(text "USB to anyone who wants it,\npower if it's better than what we have"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 48.26 25.146 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "40d1e14a-c3b4-4ed3-9f5b-b679796b64fc")
	)
	(text "1.49uH calc for 3.3, 2.2 ok? yolo boi"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 139.192 141.224 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
		)
		(uuid "89cd761a-3290-4bd4-914e-cab60e70c7bf")
	)
	(text "Fsw is 10^5 / Rfs (in kOhm)\nLets say 2M, small(er) inductors\n=> 470R -> 2.12M\nthat'll do"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 77.47 187.706 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
				(thickness 0.1588)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "9480c1b0-1d40-4dbc-9bab-a7866cc12cf0")
	)
	(text "eh, esp32 wants them, so be it"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 171.704 66.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
		)
		(uuid "94abde92-0e76-482e-913f-b7659561c0ef")
	)
	(text "2 for 5v and 3 for 12v, 2.2 should be fine, yolo"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 221.996 87.376 0)
